Description: CVE-2026-109618 and CVE-2026-109619 for PHP 5.6: the official EOL fix "Avoid state corruption via bailout" (PHP 7.4) carried over to the PHP 5 engine: fatal errors of the allocator (memory limit, integer overflow in allocation sizes, string size overflow in concatenation, Balloc) print and _exit() the worker instead of a zend_error() longjmp() out of a half-initialized request; state that an error before the next request startup can reach is reset (user error and exception handler stacks, error handling mode, exception, freed $_GET/$_POST/... pointers, SAPI request strings and header callback, modules_activated, the autoload guard table, zend_llist head and tail); multipart parsing keeps only Content-Disposition and Content-Type headers, without duplicates; session upload progress stays off whatever session.upload_progress.enabled says. $_GET, $_POST, $_COOKIE and their sub-arrays start as the smallest array (2 buckets: nTableMask 0 marks an uninitialized table in PHP 5), as the singleton arrays of the official fix, so that request variables cost as little memory as they can. Left out, as PHP 5 has no counterpart: HT_HASH_RESET of the PHP 7 hash tables; the CONCAT overflow checks of the PHP 7 VM are those of concat_function() here. Cross-checked with the independent 5.6 port of Ondrej Sury (php5.6 5.6.40-104, debian/patches/0261-Avoid-state-corruption-via-bailout.patch), which brought the singleton arrays, the reset of SG(callback_func) and the earlier reset of EG(error_handling) and EG(exception), and with the one of vperetti/php-cve-2026-109618-109619-backports (patches/php-5.6-CVE-2026-109618-109619.patch), which brought the reset of EG(in_autoload).
Origin: azsupport, port of php-src commit 802c21075308 (PHP 7.4, Arnaud Le Blanc, 18.10.2026, cherry-pick of b62095c75da7; GHSA-w8hw-w9fx-j79w, GHSA-6wmf-4rv5-p3rp) to remicollet PHP-5.6-security-backports-openssl11 @ 5c2cc46b45cf; replaces backport-oom-exit.patch. Drop when that branch gets its own fix

